WEBVTT

00:01.220 --> 00:03.560
<i>It's the beginning of a new year!</i>

00:04.010 --> 00:08.160
<i>Nii-chan, I'm... being tested.</i>

00:09.000 --> 00:17.860
<i>Usagi-san gave me an Atami hot spring travel voucher as Christmas present, and we decided to go there on 15th January.</i>

00:18.500 --> 00:22.690
Hotel voucher for Atami Onsen *Ryori Ryokan
Valid   12/30 ~ 8/31
Guests with this ticket may use any and all services, including lodging; breakfast, lunch, dinner; and all hotel facilities. 

00:18.500 --> 00:22.690
*Ryori Ryokan: a ryokan, or traditional Japanese inn, specialising in gourmet cuisine.<b></b>

00:18.700 --> 00:24.400
<i>but for some reason, both the elder Usagi and Usagi father gave me complimentary tickets that are also only valid on the 15th.</i>

00:23.360 --> 00:24.530
Elder Usagi

00:23.360 --> 00:24.530
Tropical Island Resort Ticket

00:25.340 --> 00:27.410
Usagi father

00:25.340 --> 00:27.410
56th National Bear Woodcarving Exhibition and Sale

00:27.860 --> 00:31.160
That's right, since this is a rare opportunity...

00:32.660 --> 00:33.970
What was that?

00:35.380 --> 00:36.500
Nothing at all!

00:37.140 --> 00:39.080
<i>What a small hearted man!</i>

00:39.740 --> 00:42.720
Of-Of course, I'm going with this...

00:43.000 --> 00:44.210
Is that so!

00:47.180 --> 00:50.600
How do I turn down the other two?

00:50.840 --> 00:52.260
Just ignore them.

00:52.400 --> 00:54.260
Like I can do that.

00:54.620 --> 00:56.810
More importantly, are you okay with your work?

00:57.200 --> 00:59.540
I've finished everything perfectly this time.

01:00.560 --> 01:01.600
Really now.

01:01.760 --> 01:03.810
There are those rare times, huh.

01:04.000 --> 01:05.800
When things need to be done, I <i>do</i> complete them.

01:06.970 --> 01:08.400
<i>Do that every time.</i>

01:09.490 --> 01:10.060
Hm?

01:11.090 --> 01:11.570
Yes?

01:11.680 --> 01:13.600
Is that Takahashi-sama?

01:13.900 --> 01:15.600
It is good to see you again.

01:15.840 --> 01:17.960
Is Akihiko-sama available?

01:18.860 --> 01:21.220
<i>It's Sebastian-san from Usagi-san's house!</i>

01:21.980 --> 01:26.970
Hate the sin but love the sinner

01:27.280 --> 01:32.530
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

01:27.280 --> 01:32.530
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

01:30.230 --> 01:43.500
Junjou Romantica 2

01:32.530 --> 01:36.000
ima futari no story

01:32.530 --> 01:36.000
Now, our story...

01:37.290 --> 01:44.780
bokura no mirai ga kagayaite yuku yo

01:37.290 --> 01:44.780
Our future is going to shine on.

01:48.220 --> 01:53.510
mae ni susumeba dareka to butsukatte

01:48.220 --> 01:53.510
If I try to move forward, I collide with someone else,

01:53.980 --> 01:58.340
okubyou ni naru bakari

01:53.980 --> 01:58.340
and always lose my nerve.

01:58.340 --> 02:03.940
dakedo mae wo muite aruite iku yo

01:58.340 --> 02:03.940
But I'm going to face front and walk ahead,

02:03.940 --> 02:07.570
kimi to aeru nara

02:03.940 --> 02:07.570
if it means I can see you.

02:09.600 --> 02:14.580
ame ni utarete furueru koe

02:09.600 --> 02:14.580
Your trembling voice, pelted by the rain,

02:14.910 --> 02:20.180
nemurenu yoru wo samayottemo

02:14.910 --> 02:20.180
even if I have to wander sleepless nights,

02:20.860 --> 02:23.660
boku wa yuku yo

02:20.860 --> 02:23.660
I'll go,

02:23.660 --> 02:30.410
kimi to deaeru sono hima de

02:23.660 --> 02:30.410
Until the day when I can see you.

02:31.230 --> 02:36.420
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

02:31.230 --> 02:36.420
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

02:36.420 --> 02:40.130
ima futari no story

02:36.420 --> 02:40.130
Now, our story

02:40.290 --> 02:41.940
ugokidashita

02:40.290 --> 02:41.940
has started.

02:41.940 --> 02:46.930
meguriatta shougeki de iro no nai sekai ga

02:41.940 --> 02:46.930
The impact of our meeting, shocked this dull, grey world

02:46.930 --> 02:54.120
isshun de azayaka ni irozuite yuku yo

02:46.930 --> 02:54.120
and instantly burst into a brilliant color.

02:59.060 --> 03:02.300
Due to the chairman's death at the end of last year,

03:02.660 --> 03:07.580
it has been decided that a formal family meeting will be held to discuss the distribution of inheritance property.

03:07.820 --> 03:11.780
I already said on the phone that I give up all my rights of inheritance.

03:12.500 --> 03:14.900
I'm afraid that is not sufficient.

03:15.210 --> 03:20.130
To give up your rights, you must still follow formal procedures that require you to be physically present.

03:20.520 --> 03:23.080
So, when is this family meeting?

03:23.520 --> 03:25.760
On 15th of January.

03:26.040 --> 03:29.220
Oh, then it's not possible for me, right Misaki?

03:29.420 --> 03:30.050
Eh?

03:30.420 --> 03:31.660
Oh, it's okay.

03:31.840 --> 03:33.840
I don't mind heading to the inn by myself-

03:34.570 --> 03:35.920
U-Uh.

03:36.380 --> 03:38.850
Do you have prior business on that day?

03:39.040 --> 03:42.060
Yes. It's an extremely urgent trip.

03:42.440 --> 03:45.300
Uh, it doesn't have to be that day.

03:45.300 --> 03:47.960
I don't have any other free day in my schedule.

03:48.400 --> 03:51.090
And I've already made reservations at the inn on that day.

03:51.380 --> 03:52.500
<i>And when was that?</i>

03:53.250 --> 04:01.440
In that case, I will ask master if the meeting could be moved from afternoon to morning.

04:02.680 --> 04:06.730
Will you be able to attend the meeting then and go to your destination afterwards?

04:07.300 --> 04:08.530
What do you think, Takahashi-sama?

04:08.530 --> 04:10.100
Eh? Oh, yes.

04:10.360 --> 04:12.200
I'm absolutely okay with it.

04:12.280 --> 04:14.940
That's right! You should do that, Usagi-san.

04:15.400 --> 04:15.940
Okay?

04:16.930 --> 04:18.140
January 15

04:18.930 --> 04:22.780
<i>As always, it's not even funny how ridiculous this estate is.</i>

04:23.380 --> 04:25.100
<i>Oh, that's the elder Usagi!</i>

04:25.240 --> 04:27.100
<i>Oh! And Kaoruko-san too!</i>

04:27.180 --> 04:33.040
<i>I see, this is a family meeting, that means all those people here belong to the Usami family.</i>

04:35.100 --> 04:36.400
Yohoo!!

04:37.820 --> 04:39.420
<i>Usagi's father!!</i>

04:41.760 --> 04:43.320
Good morning.

04:45.060 --> 04:47.960
I noticed you when I came out to welcome everyone.

04:48.370 --> 04:49.450
What's up?

04:49.770 --> 04:56.640
Oh, after this, me and Usa-... Akihiko-san are going to go to a hot spring.

04:56.780 --> 04:57.890
And...

04:58.640 --> 05:02.050
I'm sorry that I can't go to the wood carving exhibition.

05:02.260 --> 05:04.340
We had already made plans for today.

05:05.000 --> 05:07.580
Oh yes, I heard from my butler.

05:07.810 --> 05:10.200
It's okay. Don't let it bother you.

05:10.980 --> 05:14.170
<i>This feels a bit awkward. Because...</i>

05:14.780 --> 05:17.820
You are quite a troublesome existence, you see.

05:19.050 --> 05:24.860
<i>But, it looks like he isn't bothered... or rather, has he already forgotten what he said then?</i>

05:25.400 --> 05:29.940
Hot spring, eh? I sure would like to go too! Which one are you going to?

05:30.040 --> 05:32.620
Huh? Oh, in Atami.

05:32.700 --> 05:38.730
Atami! But, you see, after this meeting I have another appointment at the office.

05:39.420 --> 05:42.860
Master, everyone has gathered.

05:43.490 --> 05:44.650
Yes, yes.

05:45.580 --> 05:46.650
See you.

05:46.760 --> 05:48.300
Enjoy your trip.

05:48.410 --> 05:49.620
Oh, yes.

05:53.460 --> 05:54.680
Takahashi-kun.

05:55.450 --> 05:59.850
Akihiko is really quite attached to you, isn't he?

06:00.730 --> 06:06.280
<i>This person... hasn't forgotten about the other day.</i>

06:13.850 --> 06:17.650
This is bad! Something terrible happened! We must hurry!

06:18.250 --> 06:21.380
I forgot to finish something I was working on.

06:21.900 --> 06:23.140
Whaat!!!

06:26.060 --> 06:27.720
So then, let's go! To Atami!

06:27.720 --> 06:29.720
Let's not!!

06:30.340 --> 06:33.520
Where the hell are you!!? What happened to your job!!?

06:36.220 --> 06:40.940
Hello? I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry! He's seriously an idiot! I'm sorry!!!

06:40.940 --> 06:42.640
Tell her not to worry.

06:42.770 --> 06:47.120
While leaving the house, because I felt a bit uneasy, I brought my computer with me.

06:47.410 --> 06:49.120
No use saying that!!

06:51.600 --> 06:52.960
It's the ocean!!

06:53.620 --> 06:54.740
Do you like it?

06:54.970 --> 06:55.770
Yeah!

06:56.040 --> 07:00.520
But, I couldn't believe that this ticket covered reserving a private guest house.

07:01.820 --> 07:05.520
Oh hey, are things with your family okay now?

07:05.720 --> 07:10.000
Yeah. Apparently, my grandfather had left me a little something, just for pocket money.

07:10.340 --> 07:12.000
I told them that I don't want it.

07:12.530 --> 07:16.570
What's this? If it was only pocket money, you should have just accepted it.

07:16.880 --> 07:17.720
How much was it?

07:18.130 --> 07:19.220
1.3 billion.

07:19.360 --> 07:23.610
1.3 billion!!!? Just accept it!!! No matter what happens you just have to accept it!!

07:23.680 --> 07:24.370
I won't.

07:24.450 --> 07:25.400
Why!!?

07:25.680 --> 07:27.840
I could make that much myself, that's why.

07:28.440 --> 07:31.380
<i>Nii-chan, I just felt the urge to kill...</i>

07:31.660 --> 07:32.490
What's wrong?

07:37.900 --> 07:40.640
Usagi-san, I'll head out for a bath.

07:40.770 --> 07:44.060
Hm? You could just the open-air bath outside our room.

07:44.460 --> 07:48.170
No. Since it's such a rare chance, it's got to be the big bathhouse first.

07:50.970 --> 07:53.490
Big baths really are the best!

07:53.960 --> 07:57.130
Usagi-san is doing his work seriously.

07:57.570 --> 07:59.810
I can't be a bother to him.

08:07.370 --> 08:08.490
Good day.

08:10.840 --> 08:14.280
Shhh. There are other guests here too.

08:16.200 --> 08:18.220
S-Sorry...

08:18.570 --> 08:24.000
I never had the chance to use them, so I thought I'd use them here.

08:24.450 --> 08:28.520
Excuse me, but you said you had a meeting at the office.

08:29.000 --> 08:33.880
Yes. But I just couldn't resist when I heard the word "hot spring".

08:34.560 --> 08:38.560
So, I decided that I'd just hold the meeting at this inn.

08:38.730 --> 08:40.400
Is that so...?

08:41.020 --> 08:43.680
<i>Would someone normally do that?</i>

08:44.060 --> 08:45.680
Everything just now was a lie.

08:45.920 --> 08:49.580
To tell the truth, I came here to have a talk with you.

08:49.850 --> 08:50.840
<i>As I thought.</i>

08:51.650 --> 08:54.690
Oh, you don't have to be on guard like that.

08:54.960 --> 08:58.140
I really just wanted to have a talk with you.

08:59.010 --> 09:04.160
About the bear wood carvings and uh, wood carvings... and wood carvings...

09:04.440 --> 09:05.300
Okay.

09:05.480 --> 09:08.360
And also, about my son.

09:10.560 --> 09:12.690
You see, I'm quite curious.

09:12.740 --> 09:17.480
You two aren't close in age either, so how did you come to know each other.

09:18.610 --> 09:21.940
My elder brother was his classmate in high school, that's how we met.

09:21.940 --> 09:24.010
Oh, I see.

09:24.360 --> 09:27.680
And for how long have you be living together?

09:28.010 --> 09:29.680
Since last April.

09:30.320 --> 09:37.490
My brother got transferred all of a sudden for work. And so Usagi-san asked if I'd like to stay with him.

09:37.820 --> 09:40.170
Eh? Akihiko said that?

09:40.340 --> 09:41.700
Uh-yes.

09:42.080 --> 09:43.340
I see.

09:44.100 --> 09:49.610
As his parent, I have noticed that Akihiko always had a tendency to distance himself from others.

09:49.960 --> 09:52.330
It was much worse when he was younger.

09:53.340 --> 09:59.570
How to say this... he absorbs other people's emotions and actions much more than he should.

10:00.250 --> 10:03.400
You could say, he's more fragile than a normal person...

10:04.220 --> 10:10.090
He did make friends, but I thought it was impossible for him to live together with anyone.

10:10.680 --> 10:16.040
I've heard that from many people, but I'm getting along just fine.

10:16.300 --> 10:17.260
Really...?

10:17.520 --> 10:20.840
Deep down, Usagi-san is a really kind person.

10:21.160 --> 10:25.720
Hm... but kindness is also the flip side of weakness.

10:27.180 --> 10:31.100
It's good that he has found an outlet through his writing,

10:31.800 --> 10:36.050
but his fundamental fragility will never really disappear, you see.

10:37.290 --> 10:43.210
Well, in the end, I just wish for my son to be happy.

10:44.050 --> 10:46.240
Yes. I understand.

10:46.740 --> 10:47.930
Do you?

10:49.060 --> 10:54.370
I'm saying, that I will have a problem if you are in this half-heartedly.

10:55.940 --> 10:57.930
You're a very good kid.

10:58.690 --> 11:01.820
But, I don't need a kid who's only good on the surface.

11:03.130 --> 11:06.260
Sorry. It's almost time for my meeting.

11:06.900 --> 11:08.120
Excuse me.

11:08.840 --> 11:12.200
Oh and please feel free to keep the duckies if you like.

11:12.960 --> 11:14.810
Give my regards to Akihiko.

11:17.930 --> 11:23.730
<i>Why does his father have to say things like I'm a problematic existence or I have half-hearted attitude?</i>

11:25.060 --> 11:28.460
<i>If Usagi-san is with me, will he become unhappy?</i>

11:28.960 --> 11:32.080
<i>That's something only Usagi-san can decide.</i>

11:33.020 --> 11:39.080
<i>Besides, who was the one who took in a sound, healthy 19 year old boy and led him astray?</i>

11:40.290 --> 11:47.490
<i>Could it be, that his father was trying to say, that this way of thinking would cause trouble for Usagi-san?</i>

11:48.170 --> 11:51.570
<i>If that's so, what should I do?</i>

11:52.380 --> 11:57.800
<i>Maybe the reason I've been feeling this resentment, is because I've been averting my eyes from the problem.</i>

11:59.440 --> 12:04.100
<i>If I really want this to work out, I've got to think by myself.</i>

12:13.320 --> 12:14.450
You idiot.

12:14.930 --> 12:18.160
Who's stupid enough these days to stay in the bath till they pass out?

12:18.320 --> 12:19.900
Is that guy okay?

12:18.850 --> 12:21.020
Oh no! Someone drowned here!

12:21.420 --> 12:23.520
Oh yeah, there's one here.

12:23.970 --> 12:25.680
And whose fault do you-?

12:27.320 --> 12:28.760
<i>Not good.</i>

12:29.000 --> 12:29.770
You.

12:31.640 --> 12:34.000
You've been hiding something lately, haven't you?

12:34.050 --> 12:35.220
Not really.

12:36.100 --> 12:37.220
That's a lie, right?

12:37.760 --> 12:40.920
Enough about me, get back to your work.

12:41.720 --> 12:44.090
I've made good progress, so it's fine.

12:44.500 --> 12:46.160
I'm talking about you right now.

12:46.530 --> 12:48.620
I said, it's nothing!

12:49.090 --> 12:51.000
You know what happens if you won't say anything?

12:51.340 --> 12:51.860
What?

12:51.860 --> 12:54.140
Akihiko pressed his and Misaki's...

12:55.440 --> 12:57.770
Why did you bring something like that with you?

12:57.770 --> 12:58.600
No. Ah.

12:58.720 --> 13:02.020
I got it! I get it already!! Don't read it out loud!!!

13:04.980 --> 13:07.610
Why do you keep everything to yourself?

13:08.970 --> 13:15.500
Just realize already, all your efforts of trying not to worry me, end up making me worried all the more.

13:15.890 --> 13:18.980
Please, cause more trouble for me.

13:21.360 --> 13:25.380
At the end of last year, when all that stuff with Kaoruko-san happened,

13:25.380 --> 13:28.890
I met your brother alone, remember?

13:29.130 --> 13:34.250
Actually, after that, coincidentally, I met your father as well.

13:34.660 --> 13:41.490
I was told not stay with you... or something along those lines, by him.

13:41.780 --> 13:44.180
And just now I met him in the bath as well.

13:44.410 --> 13:47.500
What? I thought he was supposed to be in Tokyo for work.

13:47.810 --> 13:51.250
Yeah. he said they would be having their meeting at this inn.

13:51.560 --> 13:58.140
Just then, he told me he didn't want me to stay beside you with half-hearted feelings.

13:58.570 --> 14:01.890
But you know, I've thought about a lot of things too!

14:02.320 --> 14:07.640
Like paying the rent to lessen my burden on you, even if it's only by a little bit.

14:08.020 --> 14:11.080
And make sure I never create a uneasy atmosphere.

14:12.020 --> 14:16.210
And if your father is concerned about your public image,

14:16.600 --> 14:20.160
then I could keep a low profile so as to not stand out as much as possible.

14:20.330 --> 14:25.820
Besides, I'm working really hard part-time right now, so that I can live on my own.

14:26.690 --> 14:31.500
But, if I'm not there, you might really end up dead somewhere.

14:32.090 --> 14:36.940
But then again, when I wasn't there, you were living perfectly fine too.

14:37.280 --> 14:41.720
Then I wondered, why am I living with Usagi-san?

14:42.220 --> 14:45.730
Because of that, I sort of got lost in everything.

14:47.000 --> 14:51.490
<i>Maybe, it's just that I wanted to be with him all along.</i>

14:51.930 --> 14:53.250
Are you stupid?

14:53.810 --> 14:54.440
Eh?

14:54.570 --> 14:55.560
Useless.

14:56.330 --> 14:57.560
Useless you say!

14:58.420 --> 14:59.560
It's alright.

15:00.440 --> 15:01.450
What is?

15:02.010 --> 15:03.450
Everything.

15:08.680 --> 15:09.930
What's up with you?

15:09.930 --> 15:13.500
<i>I don't understand one bit how everything's fine.</i>

15:14.180 --> 15:17.640
<i>But I felt like my feelings just got sorted a bit just now.</i>

15:18.970 --> 15:22.930
Was it good... that I talked?

15:25.170 --> 15:27.650
Hello? Oh, Aikawa-san.

15:28.100 --> 15:31.380
If you want Usagi-san, he just went out for some cigarettes...

15:32.080 --> 15:33.700
Oh yeah, he sure is late.

15:34.480 --> 15:35.410
Man...

15:35.720 --> 15:38.330
Just how far did he go to buy cigarettes anyway?

15:37.000 --> 15:38.940
Let's play ping-pong!

15:39.130 --> 15:40.220
We will later, okay?

15:40.380 --> 15:42.040
Oh, Usagi-san-

15:42.330 --> 15:44.440
I won't take much of your time.

15:46.370 --> 15:47.810
Should we sit down for a bit?

15:49.660 --> 15:52.440
<i>Usagi's father! Why are they together?</i>

15:52.920 --> 15:55.380
<i>Could it be because of me?</i>

15:57.290 --> 16:00.130
I don't understand what you are thinking, but

16:01.490 --> 16:04.360
I wish you wouldn't do anything unnecessary.

16:04.970 --> 16:06.960
How should I say this...

16:07.420 --> 16:11.560
He's such an ordinary boy that I was just thrown off balance a bit.

16:12.330 --> 16:14.940
I do believe I know you very well.

16:16.000 --> 16:18.720
I am your father after all.

16:19.660 --> 16:25.900
Since a long time ago, whenever you lost your belongings, you'd be much more hurt than others would.

16:27.040 --> 16:32.400
And every time that happened, you just shut your heart to everyone and everything.

16:32.850 --> 16:34.820
That's all from when I was a child.

16:35.250 --> 16:36.260
Really?

16:36.650 --> 16:41.050
I don't want to see that happen to you again, you see.

16:41.400 --> 16:43.980
Takahashi-kun is a perfectly ordinary boy.

16:44.220 --> 16:46.420
I'm not saying that being ordinary is bad,

16:48.240 --> 16:54.850
still, a person's values are dictated by the environment in which they were raised.

16:54.920 --> 16:59.220
And in that respect, both you and him have very little in common. Don't you agree?

17:01.210 --> 17:04.700
I, myself, was a commoner who married into the Usami family,

17:04.850 --> 17:07.440
so I understand how this works, much better than you.

17:07.960 --> 17:10.040
Reality is harsh.

17:10.420 --> 17:14.800
All may be well right now, but one day, you'll definitely become a burden to each other.

17:15.660 --> 17:20.490
<i>Usagi's father said that he wanted Usagi-san to be happy.</i>

17:21.690 --> 17:25.580
<i>Maybe, this is something only a parent could know, but...</i>

17:26.170 --> 17:27.050
<i>Still!</i>

17:28.040 --> 17:30.730
Well, I've heard everything till the end.

17:31.320 --> 17:33.500
Is that all you wanted to say?

17:34.300 --> 17:36.800
Should I be explicit, so that it's easily understandable?

17:37.360 --> 17:38.880
I don't mind if you're just playing around.

17:39.320 --> 17:44.970
However, if you are serious, then I don't think you and Takahashi-kun are suited for each other.

17:48.080 --> 17:50.200
What are you doing here?

17:50.690 --> 17:52.330
E-Eavesdropping.

17:52.840 --> 17:54.460
Oh dear!

18:00.210 --> 18:02.380
Please don't just say things as you like!

18:03.120 --> 18:08.010
It's true, that right now I might not be good enough for Usagi-san in a lot of ways, but

18:08.450 --> 18:13.320
I intend to work hard to improve myself, that was my plan from the beginning!

18:13.700 --> 18:17.410
I, too, am not in this with half-hearted feelings!

18:17.640 --> 18:18.490
And also-

18:18.650 --> 18:22.970
Specifically, just how long and what are you going to work hard on?

18:24.970 --> 18:26.200
That...

18:26.690 --> 18:30.700
Excuse me. Would you stop driving this conversation however you like?

18:33.080 --> 18:33.980
It's okay.

18:35.760 --> 18:38.400
Have you read my recent novels?

18:38.800 --> 18:42.570
Yes I have. Every single one since your debut.

18:42.840 --> 18:45.520
Is there anything you've noticed?

18:46.040 --> 18:46.770
Hm?

18:47.120 --> 18:53.810
Till now, my books used to have a lonely, savage view of the world, but

18:54.120 --> 18:57.980
I've been told many times recently, that it's become kinder.

18:59.810 --> 19:03.290
That made me incredibly happy.

19:06.610 --> 19:09.250
All of that, is thanks to him.

19:12.960 --> 19:15.930
This is my only answer.

19:16.260 --> 19:17.050
Let's go.

19:17.860 --> 19:19.650
Work hard, huh?

19:20.020 --> 19:22.420
I do think those are very nice words, but

19:22.900 --> 19:27.100
thinking that your hard work will pay off 100% is

19:27.490 --> 19:29.100
impossible.

19:32.240 --> 19:34.170
Hey! What do you think you're-

19:40.660 --> 19:43.370
Don't be bothered by what my father said.

19:45.720 --> 19:51.250
No matter what anyone says, I don't intend to let go of you.

19:54.410 --> 19:58.860
Hey! In a place like this! Stop! Stop it! Don't touch me!

19:58.860 --> 20:00.540
You mean, "touch me more!"

20:01.440 --> 20:03.720
<i>Taking us being together for granted,</i>

20:04.280 --> 20:07.210
<i>and how we touch each other's bodies like this more and more...</i>

20:07.760 --> 20:11.840
<i>and really believing that everything is alright when Usagi-san says so,</i>

20:13.800 --> 20:16.560
<i>I could almost fall under an illusion.</i>

20:17.180 --> 20:19.280
No...! Don't move!

20:19.280 --> 20:22.180
Misaki, fall in love with me.

20:22.840 --> 20:26.900
Love me 10 times, 20 times more than you do now,

20:27.160 --> 20:30.100
till you can no longer bear to be away from me.

20:32.530 --> 20:34.820
You doing just that is enough.

20:35.200 --> 20:42.340
No matter what anyone says, or tries to do, I will absolutely protect you.

20:44.450 --> 20:45.530
<i>Usagi-san...</i>

20:47.180 --> 20:49.370
<i>Usagi-san is kind.</i>

20:50.050 --> 20:53.080
<i>So kind, that it makes me want to cry.</i>

21:05.740 --> 21:10.880
Yokogiru dake wa ichinichi no owari ni

21:05.740 --> 21:10.880
Crossing paths at the end of the day,

21:11.010 --> 21:16.270
itsu kara ka kimi ga sakimawari shite matte ite

21:11.010 --> 21:16.270
at some point you went up ahead and waited for me.

21:16.620 --> 21:21.640
ureshii kimochi bai ni shite kurete

21:16.620 --> 21:21.640
You doubled all my happiness,

21:21.640 --> 21:28.330
kanamishi kimochi hanbun ni shite kureru kara

21:21.640 --> 21:28.330
and halved all my sadness.

21:28.440 --> 21:33.440
kore kara donna michi aruitemo

21:28.440 --> 21:33.440
No matter what path I walk in the future,

21:33.840 --> 21:38.120
kitto sore wa kimi he to tsuzuiteru

21:33.840 --> 21:38.120
will surely lead to you.

21:38.120 --> 21:40.880
boku no saki ni wa kimi ga ite

21:38.120 --> 21:40.880
You're there up ahead of me,

21:40.880 --> 21:43.740
kimi no saki ni wa boka ga iru

21:40.880 --> 21:43.740
I'm there ahead of you,

21:43.740 --> 21:49.010
hoka no dare mo inai futari dake no basho

21:43.740 --> 21:49.010
A place for just the two of us with no one else around.

21:49.010 --> 21:54.910
sore ga boku no subete nanda sore ga boku wo karuku shiteru na

21:49.010 --> 21:54.910
That's my everything, and lifts the weight off my shoulders.

21:55.500 --> 21:59.980
mou doko he mo ikanaide

21:55.500 --> 21:59.980
Hey, don't go anywhere.

21:59.980 --> 22:05.440
yakusoku no basho wa itsumo hidamari no kaori wo sasete

21:59.980 --> 22:05.440
Our promised place always has the smell of sunshine.

22:05.440 --> 22:10.830
boku no ashimoto wo terashiteirunda

22:05.440 --> 22:10.830
It's casting a light at my feet.

22:10.830 --> 22:16.650
kimi no koto ga suki da yotte to ieru boku ga suki dakara

22:10.830 --> 22:16.650
I love myself being able to say "I love you!"

22:17.040 --> 22:22.330
mune no oku de sotto arigatou

22:17.040 --> 22:22.330
Softly in my heart I say, "Thank you."

22:25.850 --> 22:26.600
Misaki.

22:27.070 --> 22:28.050
Go on ahead.

22:28.600 --> 22:28.970
Okay.

22:29.840 --> 22:33.850
<i>Even though I went to a hot spring, why does my body feel so heavy.</i>

22:36.820 --> 22:39.440
<i>I wonder if Usagi's father has already gone back.</i>

22:40.170 --> 22:43.160
<i>I do believe Usagi-san will really protect me every single time.</i>

22:43.580 --> 22:45.500
<i>But that's not good.</i>

22:46.160 --> 22:48.320
<i>Don't run away. Face him properly.</i>

22:48.600 --> 22:51.390
<i>I've got to build up the confidence to argue back properly.</i>

22:54.740 --> 22:56.330
Something terrible has happened!

22:56.540 --> 22:57.060
What?

22:57.600 --> 22:59.010
<i>Did his father again-!?</i>

22:59.820 --> 23:05.270
I was so absorbed in you that I forgot to complete the story I was writing.

23:05.830 --> 23:06.640
Whaat!?

23:09.300 --> 23:12.320
Anyway, since we've come all the way to Atami,

23:12.320 --> 23:16.200
wouldn't you agree that Hamamatsu is a stone's throw away?

23:16.820 --> 23:17.380
What!?

23:18.260 --> 23:20.100
What happened to the damn manuscript!!?

23:20.100 --> 23:22.150
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!!

23:22.150 --> 23:24.620
I just got this urge to eat eel while gazing at Mt. Fuji.

23:24.620 --> 23:26.010
Let's go! To Hamamatsu!

23:26.010 --> 23:26.970
Sensei!!

23:26.970 --> 23:28.400
Everything is Misaki's fault.

23:28.400 --> 23:30.260
Don't involve me in this!!!

23:30.480 --> 23:34.170
Nii-chan, saying Usagi-san is really kind... I take it all back!!!

23:35.020 --> 23:45.020
Raws: BDRIP (from nyaa.se)
Translation: aarinfantasy
Timing, Typesetting, Minor script editing and Encoding: asckj1

23:57.080 --> 24:00.090
All's well that ends well
